SQL> prompt === deploy application contexts ===
=== deploy application contexts ===
SQL> 
SQL> -- The USING clause is the security control, not decoration: it names the only package permitted to
SQL> -- write this namespace, so application code cannot set its own identity by calling
SQL> -- dbms_session.set_context directly (spec-patch-06 section 6.2).
SQL> --
SQL> -- The namespace is DERIVED FROM THE SCHEMA, not fixed, because application contexts are
SQL> -- database-global objects. A fixed 'ROAD_CTX' means the second ROAD application deployed to a
SQL> -- database silently re-points the namespace at its own package, and the first one then gets
SQL> -- ORA-01031 from dbms_session on every request -- with nothing in its own repo having changed.
SQL> -- Confirmed on this ADB: deploying road-kit broke road-cal, and re-deploying road-cal broke
SQL> -- road-kit. road_ctx_pkg.namespace derives the same value at runtime.
SQL> --
SQL> -- Requires CREATE ANY CONTEXT; the drop script additionally requires DROP ANY CONTEXT. Oracle has
SQL> -- no schema-scoped equivalent of either.
SQL> declare
  2    l_namespace varchar2(30) := substr('ROAD_CTX_' || sys_context('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA'), 1, 30);
  3  begin
  4    execute immediate 'create or replace context ' || l_namespace || ' using road_ctx_pkg';
  5    dbms_output.put_line('[INFO] Context ' || l_namespace || ' created for road_ctx_pkg');
  6  end;
  7  /
[INFO] Context ROAD_CTX_ROAD_KIT_DEV created for road_ctx_pkg


PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.

